# Real statements, spreadsheets and contracts. These carry client names, CNPJs and
# balances — they stay on disk for parsing and never enter git history.
#
# No trailing slash on purpose: in a git worktree this path is a *symlink* to the real
# folder in the main checkout, and `/docs/reference/` only matches a directory, so the
# link showed up as untracked and one `git add -A` away from being committed.
/docs/reference
